<!--Post: 11369--><!--Time: 1110614013-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11369"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 11:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Alabama Sun <BR> <BR>Mobile has beach area, a stalker&#39;s dream. I&#39;m sure there are hotels on the beach like Panama City, full of women who are in a festive mood and taking more chances than they ordinarily would. Especially during spring break. <BR> <BR>There is also &#34;the original Mardi Gras&#34; durring which the cops are over-taxed and a drunk woman is never more than an arms length away.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11369-->
<!--Post: 11391--><!--Time: 1110655452-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11391"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 12, 2005 - 11:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->A little surfing on official and other AF sites turned up an AF communications training school at Keesler AFB in Biloxi. Thats 56 miles southwest of Mobile. Possibly he needed training on new types of equipment going up in the far east? Kadena is home to major communications facilities.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11391-->
<!--Post: 11400--><!--Time: 1110672004-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11400"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 12, 2005 - 4:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->How far away from the training base in Alabama Would Lewis Smith Lake be, I believe it&#39;s in north central Alabama.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11400-->
<!--Post: 11432--><!--Time: 1110701334-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11432"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bbyrum9@foothill.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 13, 2005 - 12:08 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Keesler is actually in Mississipi, about 20 miles west of the Alabama line. Lewis Smith Lake is about 40 miles North of Birmingham. It looks to be over 280 miles North of Biloxi.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11432-->
<!--Post: 11434--><!--Time: 1110703323-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11434"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 13, 2005 - 12:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ebersage, it&#39;s believed he may have been stationed sometime in the late &#39;60&#39;s at Brookley field near Mobile, Alabama. Brookley Field has long been closed down since then.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11434-->
<!--Post: 11448--><!--Time: 1110753036-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11448"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bbyrum9@foothill.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 13, 2005 - 2:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Until you can come up with Brookley&#39;s mission, I think Keesler Field is more logical, it&#39;s stated to have had a comm. training facility, and close enough to Mobile to be an easy weekend ride. Brookley closed in 1969, so it&#39;s still a possibility.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11448-->
<!--Post: 11452--><!--Time: 1110755665-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11452"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 13, 2005 - 3:14 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I keep picking up on a place named Lewis, see if you can find any place near that Base with the name Lewis attached to it please it may be important Rader met someone there or killed someone there.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11452-->
<!--Post: 11459--><!--Time: 1110765872-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11459"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bbyrum9@foothill.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 13, 2005 - 6:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nothing named Lewis within a radius of 150 miles of Mobile or Biloxi. I&#39;ll send you something tomorrow about searching place names. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11459-->
<!--Post: 11463--><!--Time: 1110768388-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11463"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 13, 2005 - 6:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks ND and when you get a chance go read the plane crash thread, interesting, since we are talking about Planes and AF<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11463-->
<!--Post: 11467--><!--Time: 1110771757-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11467"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 13, 2005 - 7:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dennis Rader was enlisted in the US Airforce at Brookley Field in Mobile, Alabama from 1967-1968. <BR>Police in Mobile are looking into their cold case files concerning these years.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11467-->
<!--Post: 11538--><!--Time: 1110895786-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11538"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 15, 2005 - 6:09 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ok from what we know so far about the plane crash and where Rader may have been I think Lewis was the name of the person. Has anyone had the time to look at the unsolved murders in Mobile Alabama in reference to the base location?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11538-->
<!--Post: 11789--><!--Time: 1111176201-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11789"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lizzie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lizzie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 18, 2005 - 12:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Military records show he was in the Air Force from 1966 to 1972, serving at bases in Texas and Mobile, Alabama. Has anyone heard anything else about Texas?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11789-->
<!--Post: 11791--><!--Time: 1111178674-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11791"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lizzie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lizzie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 18, 2005 - 12:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rader went through basic training in Lackland Air Force Base in San Antonio and later attended technical school at Sheppard Air Force Base in Wichita Falls, Texas. It is unlikely he left those bases much, if at all, during training, Soto said.  <BR> <BR> <BR>&#34;In February 1967, he was stationed at Brookley Air Force Base in Mobile, Ala., where he worked on antenna system installation and maintenance, his records show. In January 1968, Rader was based at Kadena Air Base in Okinawa, and months later went to Tachikawa Air Base in Japan.&#34; from the associated press <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11791-->
<!--Post: 11805--><!--Time: 1111195242-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11805"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:williammichael@direcway.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 18, 2005 - 5:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Looking at plane crases in the USA is a waste of time.  It is worthwhile to look for unsolved murders near any base where he spent any time. <BR>It is most likely  near Kadena and Tachikawa that the first dck victims died.  I will bet money, and I never bet money.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11805-->
<!--Post: 11823--><!--Time: 1111226402-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11823"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bbyrum9@foothill.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 19, 2005 - 2:00 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lizzie, can you prove what you are saying? That timeline does not include Greece, Turkey and Korea yet. Also, his stated release date has been Aug. 9, 1970. Are you saying that is wrong? Also, why is he at Brookley, building antennas for a base that had been scheduled to close? And that did close on 30 June, 1969?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11823-->
<!--Post: 11829--><!--Time: 1111239964-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11829"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 19, 2005 - 5:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Night, I have read that he was in the reserves after being discharged until 1972.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11829-->
<!--Post: 11842--><!--Time: 1111272380-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11842"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 19, 2005 - 2:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->O.K.MIKE- <BR> <BR>you might be right about his first killings being overseas, but what can be done about that other than extradite him to Japan to stand trial. Thats not likely. The Airforce might take away his good conduct medal, but military courts have no juristiction over him. <BR> <BR>What happened in Japan stayed in Japan...that sanpan has sailed.  <BR> <BR>Unless the PD/DA have screwed up the warrant &#40;apparently the jury is still out on that one&#41; there is evidence already to try him. The only way to get him to face the death penalty is to find killings that he has committed since 94. <BR> <BR>However in the end we are all want to know everything he did, so I&#39;m not saying that the Japanese angle is an invalid investment of time. All I&#39;m saying is that we all have our own priorities. I personally am not buying into BTK randomly targeting the Otero,s and single handedly going medieval on them in a span of 45 minutes. I hate the idea of anyone getting off , no matter how small their part in it was. <BR> <BR>Plus after reading the crash report, the flight was TOTALLY illegal. There was no flight plan, they got no weather report, nothing. They have no idea where the plane came from, it has &#40;had&#41; no home base or owner on record. Until it hit the ground, it didn&#39;t exist. So what made anyone think that it was headed for Wichita? The only thing I can think of is that they ID&#39;d one or more of the bodies as being from Wichita. <BR> <BR>They might have found some sectional charts that didn&#39;t burn all of the way, and some names and phone numbers, but I doubt that they just looked at which direction it was pointed, and decided that the plane couldn&#39;t make it past Kansas. <BR> <BR>Then they suddenly discount the whole theory &#40;in practically the same breath as they discounted Katheryn Bright as a BTK victim&#41;, then they packed their bags and head to Puerto Rico to investigate. Very little about this case makes &#39;good&#39; sense. A lot of it makes no sense.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11842-->
</table></td></tr></table>
